# tools/shape_number_witness.rish -- the START-INVARIANT, ROTATION-INVARIANT canonical form of a boundary, on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- image/chain_code.rye reads a traced ring down to a Freeman chain code that KEEPS
# orientation (a turn moves the code values, a different trace start rotates the whole string). This rung folds both freedoms
# out: the FIRST DIFFERENCE (diff[k] = (codes[k] - codes[k-1]) mod 8, cyclic) cancels rotation, and the minimum-magnitude cyclic
# rotation of that difference cancels the trace start, yielding the SHAPE NUMBER -- a canonical form that makes shape identity a
# byte compare (Bribiesca & Guzman 1980; Gonzalez & Woods). Compose not braid: this rung owns only the differencing and the
# canonical rotation; chain_code owns the code and its geometry.
#
# The crux this witness proves on metal: a 5x5 block and the same code turned 90 degrees read the IDENTICAL first difference
# while the codes differ; the shape number is invariant to turn AND trace start together (the block, the block turned-and-
# re-started, and every re-start read one number); a spread 5x2 block and its true 90-degree turn (a 2x5 block) trace to
# DIFFERENT chain codes yet share one shape number, while a block and a triangle keep DIFFERENT ones; the shape number is <=
# every cyclic rotation of the first difference (canonical minimality); degenerate cases and refusals by name. No network, no
# key, no funds -- the canonical outline a surface names the day it matches, hashes, or deduplicates a shape blind to its pose.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/shape_number_witness.rish

say "shape_number: Language EN -- Season G start-invariant, rotation-invariant canonical form over chain_code's Freeman code; first_difference cancels rotation, shape_number minimizes it over all cyclic starts to cancel the trace start, shape_number_equal makes shape identity a byte compare."
say "shape_number: Style Radiant -- compose not braid: this rung owns only the differencing and the canonical rotation; chain_code owns the code and its geometry. No gather, no blend, no codec, no color, not even a pixel-writing loop -- a reading, not a render."
say "shape_number: Lens TAME -- the minimum-rotation search is quadratic, so it carries its own hard ceiling shape_number_max_len and a longer code refuses ShapeTooLong; a value outside 0..7 refuses BadCode; all-or-nothing, never a half-built number; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/shape_number"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/shape_number.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "shape_number: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "shape_number: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "shape_number: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-shape-number" else "shape_number: selftest did not print the GREEN line"

say "shape_number: GREEN -- a block and its 90-degree turn read the identical first difference while their codes differ, the shape number is invariant to turn and trace start together, a spread block and its quarter-turn share one shape number where a triangle keeps its own, the shape number is <= every cyclic rotation of the first difference, the refusals fire by name, on metal."
